  {
    "text": "kgmodule-utils version 0.4.9, released on 2026-07-13, allows CorpusEmbedder to stream vectors to disk as shards complete, bounding peak memory by shard size rather than corpus size.",
    "topic": "memory management"
  },
  {
    "text": "The 689k-node Gutenberg consolidated build, which previously caused the parent process to exceed 10 GB RSS and trigger 45 GB of swap before being killed, can now run a single-pass on CPU after the changes in version 0.4.9.",
    "topic": "memory management"
  },
  {
    "text": "Version 0.4.9 closes the corpus-embedding memory saga by implementing streaming of vectors to disk, eliminating the need for the per-genre build workaround.",
    "topic": "memory management"
  },
  {
    "text": "Version 0.4.8 reduces the default memory footprint of parallel CPU embedding.",
    "topic": "memory management"
  },
  {
    "text": "DocKG version 0.4.6, released on 2026-07-09, lowers the default embedding batch size to prevent memory exhaustion on Apple Silicon and CPU for large knowledge graph builds.",
    "topic": "memory management"
  }
]
